# Scope (partial implementation)

The reason for a recommendation is a functional or non-functional requirement only. Ease of implementation and the amount of code are not reasons. Those are not requirements.

Do not recommend implementing only part of a path because the code is smaller or the PR is smaller. A mix of a path that is optimized and a path that is not, or a path that is supported and a path that is not, cannot be maintained.

When a task is split, plan in the same decision when the deferred part is done. The plan is a named row in `docs/roadmap.md` (ID and Issue. If it is not grilled, the status is `Set after Grill on #<n>`) or an item already under **Intentionally out of scope**. A split with neither a row nor that list is done entirely in the current Issue.

```text
# BAD — the reason is the amount of code
This row is Exact only. It fits in one PR
Sgpr later

# GOOD — choose by the requirement. If you split, put the row in the same decision
Do the same steps as f64 for f32 of Exact / Sgpr / Svgp
If you split, add the ID and Issue to the roadmap in the same change. If it is not grilled, the status is `Set after Grill on #<n>`. Write the acceptance text on the Issue
```

Adding a row is Grill → Issue (`.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc`). Do not fill the roadmap in the same turn as a question (`.cursor/rules/consent.mdc`). Write the acceptance text on the Issue. Do not copy it onto the roadmap.
